Hey, this would be cool...
Could the game be changed to add a random "contrib" level branching
off from some point in the dungeon?

For example, level 10 might have two "up" staircases; one leads back
to level 9, one to a randomly-selected "contrib" level that could be
designed locally.  The contrib levels would be in their own
subdirectory of nethackdir; perhaps a contrib.dir file in this
subdirectory would be generated to keep track of the contrib levels
and eliminate the need for nethack to scan for files.  If no contrib
files were present, the top of the staircase would be "sealed".  But
some contrib files would probably be included with the official
distribution before long.

A player would not be required to pass this level to win, so it
wouldn't matter if it was extremely hard.  It shouldn't be
instant-death-as-soon-as-you-stick-your-head-up, though, nor should it
be flooded with easy riches.

I would really enjoy this kind of outlet for creative exchange.  As
Mr. Botts said, people could post their favorite contrib levels to
this group.  The range of puzzles and interesting combinations of
dungeon features is pretty much limitless... strangely shaped rooms... 
secret doors... arrangements of traps... words spelled out in monster
letters... things written on the ground (possible in lev_comp?)...
imitations of real places like a church, the oval office, the starship
Enterprise, t(r)oll bridges...


The only problem I see with this is that it creates a score
incompatibility...  some people who put high priority on fairness will
object that the contributed level could destroy game balance and make
it very easy for someone to win.  I would say, leave it up to the
discretion of the individual.  If someone posts to the net that they
ascended in 3.1, they should confess if they got three wands of
wishing for killing a grid bug on the contrib level.  Or even if they
got a shield of reflection, if it comes standard with the level rather
than being random.

Within a multi-user site, the nethack installer could exercise some
control over the reasonableness of contrib levels, because each level
would have to be compiled and installed in a subdirectory of
nethackdir.  And different users on the same site would not have
an advantage over each other because they all have access to the
same contrib levels.
However, the designer of a level could know advantageous secrets
about it... but discovering those secrets is part of the fun.
After all, the designer only had standard nethack constructs to
work with.

Another way to help ensure fairness is that the contrib level be
accessible no earlier than dungeon level 10 or so; that way it is not
likely to create an "instant winner" game.  The player has to win their
way down to it.  By the same token, it's not as likely to instantly
kill the player, as they've had time to build up some power.

Of course, any contrib level should be thoroughly tested before
posting... otherwise you could have a lot of mad hackers at your
door...

I really like this idea because it gives players a more direct chance
to put their ideas into the game, like they can in xpilot, or
MUDs, or sokoban, ...

This would be a real kick... here's hoping!

(Btw I would be happy to write the code for this, but I don't want
to get into the code until I've ascended at least once.)

